# ShieldNet - what does not belong in the repository.
# ============================================================================
# The rule behind every line here: if a clone plus `make install` plus the Colab
# notebook can regenerate it, it is not tracked. Two things are worth being explicit
# about, because both are tempting to commit and both are mistakes:
#
#   * the dataset. 1 GB of CSVs that Kaggle already hosts, under a licence that is not
#     ours to redistribute.
#   * the trained artifact. It is a pickle of a specific library version; a reviewer who
#     checks one out six months from now gets an unpickling error rather than a model.
#     The manifest, the leaderboard and the metrics are small and reproducible, so the
#     honest way to publish a result is the number plus the config that produced it.
# ============================================================================

# -- data ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# `data/*` and not `data/`, deliberately. Git does not descend into an ignored
# *directory*, so `data/` followed by `!data/.gitkeep` silently keeps ignoring the
# .gitkeep and the empty directory never survives a clone. Ignoring the contents
# instead leaves the directory itself visible, which is what the negation needs.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
# The bundled sample the app offers in its dropdown is the one exception worth making,
# if you want a clone to demo without training. It is a few MB of the test split, and
# `shieldnet prepare --sample` regenerates it. Uncomment both lines to track it:
# !data/samples/
# !data/samples/*.csv

# -- run outputs --------------------------------------------------------------
artifacts/
reports/
*.joblib
*.pkl
*.h5
*.keras
# Optuna's study. Large, and useless without the same config and search space.
optuna.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal

# -- python -------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST
pip-log.txt
pip-delete-this-directory.txt

# -- environments -------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.python-version
.conda/

# -- test and lint caches -----------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# -- notebooks ----------------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/
# notebooks/ShieldNet_Colab.ipynb IS tracked - it is generated by
# scripts/build_colab_notebook.py and `make notebook-check` verifies the two agree.
# Anything else in notebooks/ is somebody's scratch work.
notebooks/*.ipynb
!notebooks/ShieldNet_Colab.ipynb

# -- credentials --------------------------------------------------------------
# There is no reason for a Kaggle token to be anywhere near this tree, but the cost of
# these three lines is nothing and the cost of the alternative is a rotated key.
kaggle.json
.kaggle/
*.pem
.env
.env.*
secrets.toml
# Streamlit reads .streamlit/secrets.toml. app/.streamlit/config.toml is tracked (it is
# the theme and the upload limit); a secrets file in the same directory is not.
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# -- logs and scratch ---------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
tmp/
scratch/
verdicts.csv
verdicts_*.csv

# -- editors and operating systems --------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
